index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..44efbac809d75773c9c2c72a973a6a114c2bb21d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/breakwater/apps/netbench/src/PARITY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# Blocking netbench: hardcoded versus LLVM instrumentation
+
+Both modes run the existing memory-bandwidth worker and the existing epsilon
+greedy `MemSemaphore` singleton. There are no counter or controller changes.
+The memory branch now waits unconditionally; it does not call `TryWait` or
+`WaitIfUncongested`. Other RPC overload-control policies remain in place.
+
+`memory_control.cc` defines one non-inlined, nonthrowing C-linkage boundary,
+`netbench_memory_work`. In the hardcoded build it explicitly waits, performs
+the work, and posts. In the auto build its source body only performs work;
+the LLVM pass generates the guard and dispatch slot, and the hooks wait/post.
+The worker index is read after acquisition in both builds, because a blocked
+Shenango thread can resume on another scheduler thread.
+
+`server msem` initializes the semaphore and, for auto, enables the descriptor
+before accepting requests. `server no_msem` bypasses acquisition in both modes.
+An auto build fails startup if its compiler did not prepare the function.
+The `PROFILE_ST` calibration path stays outside the instrumented boundary.
+
+The registry in `dynamic_control/` is copied from `dynamic-control` commit
+`c8e6b7b7949664a56085adfe4886eb33981b51f3`. Its header drops the unused mock
+permit-query declaration and describes the real semaphore hooks. The compiler
+ABI is unchanged. No OS-thread TLS is used for permit accounting.
+
+## Build on Linux
+
+From this directory, with Shenango's normal dependencies and libraries built:
+
+```sh
+make -f Makefile.parity MODE=hardcoded parity
+make -f Makefile.parity MODE=auto parity ir
+make -f Makefile.parity MODE=hardcoded VERIFY=1 selftest
+make -f Makefile.parity MODE=auto VERIFY=1 selftest
+```
+
+`DC_CXX` defaults to `$HOME/dynamic-control/build/llvm/bin/clang++`; override it
+with the patched Clang path if needed. Both application builds use that same
+compiler and flags. The parity Makefile targets the test machine's Zen 2 CPU,
+removing AVX-512 and user-interrupt flags. It reuses the existing runtime,
+RPC, semaphore, PCM, and NIC archives. Production binaries have no test counters.
+The ordinary Makefile builds the hardcoded blocking path as well.
+
+## Verify on amd134
+
+With the existing no-PCI iokernel running, `amd_uncore` loaded, and perf access
+available, run:
+
+```sh
+python3 run_parity.py --output /tmp/netbench-parity-results
+```
+
+The output directory must not already exist. The script uses `sudo -n` for
+Shenango applications, which need access to the configured shared memory.
+It does not restart the iokernel or change machine settings. Its single-core
+config bounds semaphore capacity at one. The tests:
+
+- Hold the only permit until all 32 user threads have queued, then execute
+  640 calls. Verify every call runs with one active permit, argument totals
+  match, acquisition/release counts balance, and the queue drains.
+- Run disabled in each build and verify the same work with no acquisitions.
+- Disable auto while a body holds a permit. Verify its release still runs,
+  the next entry bypasses hooks, and re-enabling restores acquisition.
+- Start each production netbench server with `nocontrol` and `msem`. A small
+  Linux-socket client sends 1,024 memory requests over four TCP connections,
+  in batches below the RPC slot limit. Check every response, echoed request
+  fields, and capacity; compare the deterministic response fields across builds.
+
+The network probe speaks this revision's x86-64 nocontrol wire ABI on port 8123.
+It uses the host's dtap route to the no-PCI iokernel. It is a correctness test,
+not a substitute for the original load generator or a performance measurement.
+
+## Recorded result
+
+On `hemantp@amd134.utah.cloudlab.us` (EPYC 7302P, Linux 6.8.0-149-generic),
+using patched Clang 23.1.6, all five runtime cases and both network cases passed.
+Enabled hardcoded and auto each reported 640 calls, sum 10560, 640 acquisitions,
+640 releases, and zero active permits. Disabled cases did the same work with
+zero acquisitions. The toggle case finished three calls with two balanced
+acquisitions. Each server returned all 1,024 network responses with the same
+echoed-field hash. Saved logs and source/archive/binary hashes are in
+`../parity/results/amd134/`.
+
+Remote working copy: `/users/hemantp/svalinn-shenango-dc`. The original
+`/local/shenango` deployment and its running iokernel were left in place.
+This establishes the exercised behavior at a function boundary and through
+netbench RPCs. It does not establish throughput parity or multi-core scaling.
+
+Subsequent worker and RPC measurements, with raw samples and reproduction
+commands, are recorded in `../parity/performance/amd134/RESULTS.md`.
+The multicore extension, including 2/4/8/16 scheduler-thread measurements with
+no permit TLS, is recorded in `../parity/performance/amd134/MULTICORE.md`.
